  "note": "The Tudor Great Gatehouse and moat bridge open into Base Court, with Anne Boleyn’s Gateway and the astronomical clock between it and Clock Court. The Great Hall and Chapel Royal rooflines meet the Baroque east front, Fountain Court arcades and the northern Royal Tennis Court range. The 9.2 m sea-level datum and standard terrain samples set the bridge ramp and court floor levels. The viewer mask replaces the named palace and the contained hall and chapel, keeping separate mapped buildings, paths and landscape features."
